WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.000
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:00.000 --> 00:01.660
[Disclaimer: This series is created solely for entertainment purposes.

3
00:01.680 --> 00:03.330
All individuals, behaviors, places, and events depicted are entirely fictional,

4
00:03.350 --> 00:05.000
with no intention to represent or reference any organizations, departments, occupations, or individuals]

5
00:05.120 --> 00:06.440
I'll make things right

6
00:07.000 --> 00:08.460
in three months.

7
00:08.480 --> 00:11.240
Don't you realize our relationship was never normal to begin with?

8
00:11.260 --> 00:13.640
But we still have three months to get back to how it used to be.

9
00:13.800 --> 00:15.460
So it's really you, Sun.

10
00:15.480 --> 00:17.380
Back then, you said Sun's father

11
00:17.400 --> 00:19.100
took her overseas.

12
00:19.120 --> 00:20.580
She lost her memories,

13
00:20.600 --> 00:21.680
so her father took the opportunity

14
00:21.700 --> 00:23.460
to start her life anew over there.

15
00:23.480 --> 00:25.000
I think Sun got her memories back.

16
00:28.760 --> 00:30.440
Our brains are complex.

17
00:31.120 --> 00:32.720
Chris remembers you,

18
00:33.080 --> 00:34.560
but she still had an affair.

19
00:34.820 --> 00:36.080
Perhaps...

20
00:36.460 --> 00:38.240
her memories alone aren't enough.

21
00:45.360 --> 00:46.600
You first have to know

22
00:46.860 --> 00:48.480
what Chris is planning to do.

23
00:50.680 --> 00:52.920
If I do, Chris will be mine again, right?

24
01:00.060 --> 01:01.480
Nice flowers.

25
01:02.600 --> 01:03.840
Who gave them to you?

26
01:04.200 --> 01:05.040
My friend.

27
01:06.200 --> 01:06.960
Sun...

28
01:07.440 --> 01:08.240
Who is that?

29
01:12.280 --> 01:13.700
How did you get in here?

30
01:13.720 --> 01:15.120
And who is Sun?

31
01:16.000 --> 01:18.200
A friend who helped me come up with the flower dishes.

32
01:51.480 --> 01:53.320
Whoever dares to take Chris away from me

33
01:54.120 --> 01:55.480
will die.

34
02:10.320 --> 02:20.240
♫The rain keeps splashing beneath our cover,♫

35
02:20.260 --> 02:25.360
♫Once it was a special place for two lovers♫

36
02:25.380 --> 02:29.260
♫There was never enough room for the third♫

37
02:29.480 --> 02:35.480
♫Now, the rain soaks our hearts together♫

38
02:35.500 --> 02:45.220
♫The question that's trapped in my heart♫

39
02:45.240 --> 02:50.280
♫Maybe it's time for you to do your part♫

40
02:50.300 --> 02:54.580
♫Choose the one your heart truly desires♫

41
02:54.600 --> 03:03.240
♫Before the last raindrop falls, don't make me shed another tear♫

42
03:03.760 --> 03:12.400
♫Before the last raindrop falls, don't make me shed another tear♫

43
03:53.280 --> 03:54.200
If you start,

44
03:54.220 --> 03:55.400
I won't stop you.

45
03:57.240 --> 03:58.680
No, no, no, no.

46
03:59.880 --> 04:00.840
I...

47
04:01.320 --> 04:02.600
I didn't mean to start it.

48
04:03.200 --> 04:04.320
I just...

49
04:05.760 --> 04:08.000
I just saw you were a bit exposed, so I tried to cover you up.

50
04:14.100 --> 04:15.720
I don't like people who make up excuses.

51
04:16.320 --> 04:17.880
If you want to do it, just say so.

52
04:23.440 --> 04:24.480
Oh?!

53
04:25.180 --> 04:26.160
Sorry.

54
04:27.880 --> 04:29.000
Are you hurt?

55
04:29.260 --> 04:30.880
I was just teasing you.

56
04:44.240 --> 04:45.360
That's "Kiiro",

57
04:45.960 --> 04:47.400
the one I've told you about.

58
04:49.160 --> 04:50.720
She really is yellow.

59
04:51.440 --> 04:52.360
Cute.

60
04:56.620 --> 04:57.700
I'm hungry.

61
04:57.720 --> 04:59.720
I want the hot cocoa you make on rainy days.

62
05:00.040 --> 05:01.320
It's not raining today,

63
05:01.600 --> 05:03.120
but I'll make it just for you.

64
05:59.420 --> 06:00.480
What are you looking for?

65
06:04.540 --> 06:06.280
I just wanted to tell you that I ran out of cocoa,

66
06:07.180 --> 06:09.600
but it seems like you didn't really want any.

67
06:26.820 --> 06:28.360
I locked my drawers.

68
06:28.660 --> 06:29.800
What do you want to know?

69
06:32.520 --> 06:33.560
I'm sorry.

70
06:38.900 --> 06:40.280
If you want to know something,

71
06:40.600 --> 06:41.920
just ask.

72
06:43.320 --> 06:44.600
You didn't have to lie to me.

73
06:48.480 --> 06:49.880
And are you lying to me, Sun?

74
06:52.980 --> 06:55.720
I don't think it's true that we've never known each other before.

75
06:57.840 --> 06:58.960
"Kiiro."

76
06:59.220 --> 07:00.760
It's not a very common name.

77
07:02.060 --> 07:04.960
So why do my fish and your dog have the same name?

78
07:08.200 --> 07:09.960
It's not a coincidence, right?

79
07:13.900 --> 07:15.800
Did you know me before this?

80
07:16.760 --> 07:18.280
Were we...

81
07:19.280 --> 07:21.440
more than just acquaintances?

82
07:25.180 --> 07:27.040
If we actually used to know each other,

83
07:29.780 --> 07:31.200
would anything change?

84
07:33.600 --> 07:36.160
Would you think of me differently?

85
07:37.560 --> 07:38.960
Would you still like me?

86
07:43.080 --> 07:45.080
If you're with me right now,

87
07:48.540 --> 07:50.540
it's better if we don't know each other.

88
07:55.120 --> 07:56.280
I'm sorry.

89
07:58.860 --> 08:00.600
I just want to know the truth.

90
08:04.520 --> 08:05.960
Who we are right now

91
08:07.000 --> 08:08.200
is the truth.

92
08:19.160 --> 08:20.620
It's so frustrating, Doc.

93
08:20.880 --> 08:22.720
I don't know what's real anymore.

94
08:24.320 --> 08:26.480
Didn't you say you could find the answers yourself?

95
08:29.320 --> 08:31.680
Then I'm probably all talk, like you said.

96
08:32.360 --> 08:33.660
Right now, I just want to fall asleep,

97
08:33.680 --> 08:35.840
then wake up remembering everything.

98
08:38.620 --> 08:40.620
Do you really want to remember everything again?

99
08:44.400 --> 08:46.020
Don't you remember...

100
08:46.040 --> 08:47.720
that the reason you're still alive

101
08:47.920 --> 08:49.680
is that you ran from the truth?

102
09:49.280 --> 09:51.560
Can you stop sleeping somewhere else?

103
09:52.440 --> 09:55.040
I feel like I'm going to lose you.

104
09:55.660 --> 09:57.160
Nadear, but we broke up...

105
09:57.180 --> 09:58.400
I know...

106
09:58.860 --> 10:00.960
But you said you'll give me three months.

107
10:01.960 --> 10:04.440
You can go anywhere or talk to anyone.

108
10:04.700 --> 10:06.320
I won't complain.

109
10:07.200 --> 10:08.520
But please,

110
10:09.040 --> 10:10.560
come back and sleep at home.

111
10:12.000 --> 10:14.360
Don't take away any more of my time with you.

112
10:18.120 --> 10:19.200
Okay...

113
10:19.560 --> 10:20.800
I'll try.

114
10:23.100 --> 10:24.160
Very good.

115
10:27.240 --> 10:28.200
Thank you.

116
10:32.740 --> 10:35.440
Mm... I bought you some fresh roses.

117
10:35.980 --> 10:37.980
I already put them in the vase,

118
10:38.760 --> 10:40.260
since the dried-up roses in your room

119
10:40.280 --> 10:42.000
had all fallen over.

120
11:15.040 --> 11:16.560
She probably didn't want to hurt you.

121
11:17.200 --> 11:18.280
"The truth"

122
11:18.480 --> 11:19.920
doesn't necessarily mean it'll be a good thing.

123
11:22.280 --> 11:23.960
And how is lying any better?

124
11:24.260 --> 11:26.440
Then... if you know the truth will hurt,

125
11:27.460 --> 11:28.900
are you still willing to find out?

126
11:31.680 --> 11:32.760
Chris...

127
11:34.960 --> 11:35.960
Chris...

128
11:38.480 --> 11:39.400
Chris!

129
11:40.760 --> 11:41.640
Chris!

130
11:46.940 --> 11:48.120
Chris...

131
11:50.120 --> 11:51.040
Chris.

132
11:53.660 --> 11:54.600
Chris!

133
12:10.460 --> 12:11.480
Chris.

134
12:14.440 --> 12:16.120
This one isn't an offering.

135
12:16.480 --> 12:17.960
I want to give it to you.

136
12:44.160 --> 12:45.080
Chris?!

137
12:47.240 --> 12:48.120
Chris?!

138
12:50.160 --> 12:51.360
Did you have a nightmare?

139
12:52.080 --> 12:53.260
What was it about?

140
13:04.580 --> 13:07.340
[Third Person]

141
13:09.589 --> 13:12.389
[Third Person]

142
13:14.509 --> 13:15.869
Those doors...

143
13:16.549 --> 13:18.949
will lead you to the past

144
13:19.189 --> 13:20.789
that caused you pain.

145
13:22.749 --> 13:24.349
Is that why they are locked?

146
13:24.529 --> 13:26.669
It's your body's defense mechanism.

147
13:32.049 --> 13:33.629
What if I want to go in?

148
13:35.049 --> 13:36.549
I'll guide you there.

149
13:37.109 --> 13:38.989
But are you sure...

150
13:39.309 --> 13:41.649
you want to face those painful memories?

151
14:04.109 --> 14:06.429
The reason you were in shock, lost your memories,

152
14:07.129 --> 14:09.229
and couldn't talk for a year

153
14:10.089 --> 14:13.109
was because you saw your parents pass away in the accident.

154
14:38.929 --> 14:41.869
I'm not sure if I'm ready to remember everything.

155
14:42.349 --> 14:44.349
If it's too much for you,

156
14:45.229 --> 14:47.489
you don't have to put yourself through it.

157
14:51.289 --> 14:54.069
Just let the past be the past.

158
14:55.629 --> 14:58.349
Some memories are better forgotten.

159
15:15.389 --> 15:16.789
I already told you.

160
15:17.109 --> 15:19.669
You can talk to anyone or do anything.

161
15:21.369 --> 15:24.029
I won't stop you from making those flower dishes anymore.

162
15:24.409 --> 15:25.749
You can go ahead with the promotions.

163
15:27.789 --> 15:29.549
I only ask you one thing:

164
15:30.749 --> 15:32.549
come back and sleep at our house.

165
15:47.169 --> 15:47.989
Hello,

166
15:48.429 --> 15:50.069
are you free tonight?

167
16:00.469 --> 16:01.649
Judging by that look,

168
16:01.669 --> 16:03.429
you were turned down again, weren't you?

169
16:04.989 --> 16:06.149
You know too much.

170
16:07.349 --> 16:08.949
Chris said she's going home,

171
16:09.889 --> 16:11.389
so she can't sleep with me.

172
16:12.249 --> 16:14.029
You already asked her to sleep with you,

173
16:14.229 --> 16:16.389
so why didn't you just tell her the truth at this point?

174
16:19.829 --> 16:21.389
I'll tell her after we've done more than sleep together.

175
16:22.669 --> 16:23.509
Why?

176
16:26.949 --> 16:28.609
Chris has told me...

177
16:28.629 --> 16:30.149
she had a trauma

178
16:30.169 --> 16:31.529
that made her scared of any physical touch.

179
16:32.989 --> 16:34.149
It was because of me.

180
16:36.629 --> 16:38.589
If Chris did more than sleep with you,

181
16:39.089 --> 16:40.189
would that mean...

182
16:40.589 --> 16:42.629
she got over her trauma?

183
16:44.549 --> 16:45.489
I don't know.

184
16:46.729 --> 16:47.909
But at least,

185
16:48.269 --> 16:50.549
I'll be able to forgive myself a little more.

186
16:52.549 --> 16:54.989
[Third Person Bar - Bistro]

187
17:07.149 --> 17:08.429
[Expenses]

188
17:10.229 --> 17:11.109
[Total expenses]

189
17:30.789 --> 17:31.509
Nadear,

190
17:32.529 --> 17:33.989
have you ever checked our restaurant's accounts?

191
17:34.049 --> 17:35.469
Are you still at the restaurant?

192
17:36.469 --> 17:38.129
I just got over a migraine.

193
17:38.149 --> 17:39.929
I want to know who is in charge of ordering the supplies,

194
17:39.949 --> 17:42.489
and who is managing our expenses and income.

195
17:42.509 --> 17:44.289
Can we discuss this when we're at home?

196
17:44.309 --> 17:45.029
Nadear,

197
17:45.669 --> 17:46.789
I'm serious.

198
17:47.549 --> 17:49.729
I saw that the expenses were unusually high,

199
17:49.749 --> 17:51.249
so I went back to check.

200
17:52.729 --> 17:53.929
They gradually increased

201
17:53.949 --> 17:56.189
over the past three years before I got out of the hospital.

202
17:56.629 --> 17:58.709
Normally, Nan is in charge of our stock

203
17:58.729 --> 17:59.709
and accounting.

204
18:00.509 --> 18:01.989
I did keep an eye on it from time to time.

205
18:02.469 --> 18:04.589
But our restaurant has more customers.

206
18:05.009 --> 18:06.249
When we make more income,

207
18:06.269 --> 18:08.709
it's normal for our expenses to be higher too.

208
18:08.909 --> 18:11.029
Nadear, this is very unusual.

209
18:11.709 --> 18:13.329
The prices we paid

210
18:13.349 --> 18:15.389
are a lot higher than the market price.

211
18:15.709 --> 18:17.789
I don't think Nan is stealing from us,

212
18:18.589 --> 18:20.749
but when I see these numbers, it's...

213
18:22.209 --> 18:23.469
You have to take it slow

214
18:23.749 --> 18:25.209
with Nan.

215
18:25.989 --> 18:27.429
Let me check it out.

216
18:28.209 --> 18:30.349
Don't tell Nan yet.

217
18:30.869 --> 18:32.089
Let me handle it.

218
18:40.329 --> 18:42.269
That's dangerous.

219
18:45.089 --> 18:46.829
Did I surprise you?

220
18:50.349 --> 18:51.909
One of the waiters said...

221
18:52.749 --> 18:54.149
you've been in here for a while,

222
18:55.069 --> 18:56.189
so I came to check on you.

223
18:57.429 --> 18:58.989
Is there anything I can help you with?

224
19:00.109 --> 19:00.989
So? Chris?

225
19:02.269 --> 19:03.989
Is there anything you'd like to ask me?

226
19:05.229 --> 19:07.189
Nan, holding a knife like that is dangerous.

227
19:08.509 --> 19:09.869
An object

228
19:11.229 --> 19:13.349
isn't as dangerous as the person holding it.

229
19:17.269 --> 19:17.949
Chris!

230
19:20.009 --> 19:21.369
Chris, are you still there?

231
19:32.749 --> 19:33.749
Yes, Nadear?

232
19:33.969 --> 19:35.309
You seem to be quick about this.

233
19:35.999 --> 19:37.149
Are you with Chris?

234
19:37.829 --> 19:39.389
Yeah, I'm with Chris.

235
19:40.329 --> 19:41.429
What are you two talking about?

236
19:42.709 --> 19:44.149
Just a normal conversation,

237
19:45.789 --> 19:46.549
nothing much.

238
19:50.209 --> 19:52.089
I'll tell the waiters to come clean it up.

239
20:10.589 --> 20:11.229
Chris,

240
20:12.269 --> 20:13.369
come home. Now.

241
20:17.569 --> 20:18.829
This is obviously embezzlement.

242
20:19.009 --> 20:20.129
How will you handle this?

243
20:22.309 --> 20:24.389
I told you, let me check it out first.

244
20:24.829 --> 20:26.249
Nan might have a reason

245
20:26.269 --> 20:28.149
for our expenses being higher than usual.

246
20:29.389 --> 20:31.149
No reason can justify this.

247
20:31.709 --> 20:33.889
What she did was wrong, so she needs to be held accountable.

248
20:33.909 --> 20:34.749
Chris,

249
20:35.069 --> 20:37.389
Nan had been taking care of our restaurant.

250
20:38.349 --> 20:39.229
Hey, Nadear,

251
20:39.469 --> 20:41.129
you can't use her good deeds to justify her actions,

252
20:41.149 --> 20:42.349
can you?

253
20:44.189 --> 20:47.029
Not everything is black and white in our world, Chris.

254
20:48.349 --> 20:49.909
She might not want to do us wrong,

255
20:50.189 --> 20:51.829
but something forced her to.

256
20:52.989 --> 20:55.229
Why are you trying to make me understand Nan?

257
20:56.029 --> 20:57.989
Shouldn't we discuss how to deal with this?

258
20:59.089 --> 21:00.829
Why are you siding with Nan?

259
21:01.889 --> 21:02.909
D*mn it.

260
21:03.269 --> 21:04.029
Chris!

261
21:07.289 --> 21:09.289
It's because you never understood other people.

262
21:09.589 --> 21:11.349
Everything a person chooses to do,

263
21:11.909 --> 21:12.609
whether right or wrong,

264
21:12.629 --> 21:14.909
has a reason behind it.

265
21:15.149 --> 21:16.389
It's because of money.

266
21:16.549 --> 21:17.929
She stole from us, Nadear.

267
21:17.949 --> 21:19.649
Why do you think she did that then?!

268
21:19.669 --> 21:20.909
Have you ever thought about that?!

269
21:22.569 --> 21:23.749
You never did, did you?

270
21:24.149 --> 21:26.469
Because you're obsessed with always doing what's right.

271
21:27.109 --> 21:29.369
When are you going to learn to understand other people?

272
21:34.829 --> 21:36.229
This is not working out for us.

273
21:37.469 --> 21:38.829
I don't understand you.

274
21:39.649 --> 21:40.829
And you don't understand me.

275
21:42.349 --> 21:43.989
So why are we trying to fix this?

276
21:46.589 --> 21:47.789
Let's break up.

277
21:52.949 --> 21:54.489
You don't want to break up

278
21:55.329 --> 21:56.749
because we don't understand each other.

279
21:57.909 --> 21:59.429
But you want to break up

280
22:01.809 --> 22:04.269
because you're so compatible with that new friend of yours, right?

281
22:07.309 --> 22:08.909
What did she do

282
22:09.309 --> 22:10.409
to make you like her so much

283
22:10.429 --> 22:11.869
that you stayed with her all night?!

284
22:14.769 --> 22:16.289
I can do

285
22:17.789 --> 22:19.309
what she did to you too.

286
22:40.029 --> 22:41.189
Stop it, Nadear.

287
22:41.629 --> 22:42.589
Please.

288
22:53.189 --> 22:54.849
How am I any different from her?

289
22:57.189 --> 22:59.089
Why can't it be me?

290
23:08.749 --> 23:10.389
The three months you asked me for

291
23:12.009 --> 23:14.309
won't make our situation any better.

292
23:20.609 --> 23:22.069
Let's end it here.

293
24:17.189 --> 24:21.089
♫Trapped in a love that's a fading image♫

294
24:21.109 --> 24:24.869
♫Yet the love that never faded♫

295
24:24.889 --> 24:31.369
♫Like a missing page I can't find♫

296
24:31.389 --> 24:34.369
♫Your smell lingers vividly in my mind♫

297
24:34.389 --> 24:39.629
♫The touch from when you were by my side♫

298
24:39.649 --> 24:42.469
Breaking up with her is probably for the best.

299
24:44.869 --> 24:46.949
I'll tell her that I'm moving out.

300
24:48.909 --> 24:50.989
What about the three months you promised her?

301
24:52.229 --> 24:54.789
If we keep this up, it's just going to be toxic.

302
24:58.269 --> 25:00.269
Ever since I lost my memories...

303
25:02.909 --> 25:05.549
Love became nothing more than attachment.

304
25:08.309 --> 25:10.189
Even if it's three years,

305
25:11.949 --> 25:13.669
or thirty years,

306
25:16.009 --> 25:18.469
it still won't work out.

307
25:24.629 --> 25:26.889
I don't want you to be sad like this.

308
25:31.509 --> 25:34.149
I'm not sad because I had to break up with her.

309
25:35.829 --> 25:37.629
Ever since I lost my memories...

310
25:38.949 --> 25:41.389
Love was just attachment.

311
25:54.829 --> 25:56.469
I'm just sad that...

312
26:00.309 --> 26:02.109
our relationship ended badly.

313
26:03.389 --> 26:04.809
I'm sad that...

314
26:06.549 --> 26:08.749
the person who should know me best

315
26:11.989 --> 26:13.989
doesn't understand me at all.

316
26:15.029 --> 26:17.269
If I didn't lose my memories,

317
26:18.389 --> 26:20.629
things might be a lot simpler.

318
26:24.689 --> 26:26.089
I'd be better off

319
26:26.109 --> 26:27.949
if I could remember everything.

320
26:54.469 --> 26:55.369
Chris!

321
26:58.109 --> 26:59.309
Keep it inside.

322
27:10.749 --> 27:11.349
Chris!

323
27:11.409 --> 27:12.109
Chris!

324
27:12.189 --> 27:12.989
Chris!

325
27:16.069 --> 27:17.589
You're in my room.

326
27:18.089 --> 27:19.269
It's okay.

327
27:21.469 --> 27:22.909
It was just a nightmare.

328
27:33.749 --> 27:34.549
Sun...

329
27:37.269 --> 27:38.589
you're alright now.

330
27:40.549 --> 27:41.829
I'm scared.

331
27:42.309 --> 27:43.709
I had a nightmare.

332
27:49.269 --> 27:50.109
Hm?

333
27:50.249 --> 27:51.789
Can you tell me about it?

334
28:09.309 --> 28:11.029
Which hand did you use to touch the lock?

335
28:13.509 --> 28:14.589
My right hand.

336
28:25.129 --> 28:26.509
Where were you burned?

337
28:28.469 --> 28:29.349
Sun,

338
28:29.709 --> 28:31.109
it was a nightmare.

339
28:31.349 --> 28:32.829
How could I have an injury?

340
28:40.669 --> 28:41.589
Right here.

341
28:52.089 --> 28:53.569
When you add nice things

342
28:53.789 --> 28:56.069
to bad memories

343
28:57.109 --> 28:58.789
to create new memories,

344
28:59.409 --> 29:00.509
maybe...

345
29:00.749 --> 29:02.909
your trauma can heal faster that way.

346
29:17.229 --> 29:19.469
But when I was standing in front of that door,

347
29:20.649 --> 29:21.989
I was so scared.

348
29:22.949 --> 29:24.849
I'm with you now.

349
29:25.629 --> 29:27.189
No matter where you are,

350
29:29.309 --> 29:30.869
if you have a nightmare again,

351
29:31.749 --> 29:33.709
remember this moment.

352
29:35.429 --> 29:37.029
I'll keep you company

353
29:38.289 --> 29:40.709
no matter what awaits you on the other side of that door.

354
29:57.989 --> 29:59.229
Thank you, Sun.

355
30:01.709 --> 30:03.109
But I think I know

356
30:04.349 --> 30:06.389
what's waiting for me behind that door.

357
30:15.849 --> 30:17.429
Behind that door...

358
30:18.309 --> 30:19.369
are probably my memories

359
30:19.389 --> 30:21.209
of when I lost my parents.

360
30:23.689 --> 30:26.149
It's probably because I'm scared to face that memory,

361
30:27.689 --> 30:29.269
so it became a nightmare.

362
30:32.389 --> 30:34.469
What can you remember about your parents?

363
30:39.309 --> 30:41.389
I can only recall that it was very painful.

364
30:43.629 --> 30:44.949
I was devastated.

365
30:46.889 --> 30:48.729
But I can't remember the rest.

366
30:52.609 --> 30:53.869
I only have this photo

367
30:54.149 --> 30:55.869
to remind me of what my parents looked like.

368
30:58.769 --> 31:00.789
Just thinking about looking for other photos of them

369
31:00.809 --> 31:02.149
scares me.

370
31:03.909 --> 31:05.589
Ever since the accident,

371
31:07.789 --> 31:10.189
I couldn't even bring myself to visit my parents' house.

372
31:17.989 --> 31:19.109
But if you run,

373
31:19.629 --> 31:20.829
you'll have to keep running.

374
31:23.869 --> 31:25.549
To overcome your fear,

375
31:26.869 --> 31:28.229
you'll have to face it.

376
31:31.149 --> 31:32.309
How?

377
31:36.569 --> 31:37.869
Find your memories.

378
31:58.789 --> 32:00.469
I'll stay by your side.

379
32:04.189 --> 32:07.279
[Third Person]

380
32:08.486 --> 32:12.336
[Third Person]

381
32:19.896 --> 32:21.326
I think it's here.

382
32:26.626 --> 32:27.326
Look!

383
32:27.526 --> 32:28.206
There are the horses!

384
32:28.326 --> 32:28.996
Let's go!

385
32:29.016 --> 32:29.926
Hey, wait...

386
32:31.106 --> 32:32.396
Do I have to ride the horse too?

387
32:33.016 --> 32:33.706
Don't be a chicken.

388
32:33.966 --> 32:36.626
You could do it when you were that tiny.

389
32:37.226 --> 32:38.116
Don't be scared.

390
32:39.526 --> 32:41.646
Who said I wasn't scared?

391
32:42.816 --> 32:44.766
I don't know how to ride a horse. What if I fall off?

392
32:47.316 --> 32:49.486
You are in my hands now.

393
32:50.836 --> 32:52.356
No need to be afraid.

394
32:55.086 --> 32:55.646
Let's go.

395
32:57.556 --> 32:58.526
Excuse me!

396
32:58.816 --> 33:00.036
A horse, please!

397
33:00.746 --> 33:02.116
- Are you serious? - Yes.

398
33:02.136 --> 33:02.486
Let's go.

399
33:04.486 --> 33:05.316
Is this a good idea?

400
33:10.446 --> 33:11.676
Look this way, please.

401
33:15.546 --> 33:16.836
You can go.

402
33:17.396 --> 33:19.376
Sun, didn't you say you'd go with me? Sun?!

403
33:19.646 --> 33:20.366
Bye-bye.

404
33:20.386 --> 33:21.096
Sun!

405
33:35.006 --> 33:36.606
Huh? How did you get here?

406
33:37.886 --> 33:40.056
Well, I promised to stay by your side.

407
33:41.016 --> 33:42.316
Thanks.

408
33:46.986 --> 33:47.826
Do you like it?

409
33:48.756 --> 33:49.626
Mm...

410
33:49.686 --> 33:51.086
But the horse is a bit tall.

411
34:16.406 --> 34:17.366
Are you tired?

412
34:20.696 --> 34:21.936
Do you remember anything?

413
34:24.966 --> 34:26.556
But I won't forget about today.

414
34:28.706 --> 34:30.116
Are you still scared?

415
34:33.476 --> 34:35.006
I'm not.

416
34:35.316 --> 34:37.206
It'd be much scarier if you weren't here with me.

417
34:38.916 --> 34:41.446
Thank you for staying with me.

418
34:42.426 --> 34:43.716
You're like a talisman that keeps ghosts away.

419
34:46.026 --> 34:47.006
You're crazy.

420
34:48.456 --> 34:49.716
Would you like to buy handmade necklaces?

421
34:49.736 --> 34:50.616
Are you interested?

422
34:50.646 --> 34:52.606
Would you like one? I made them all myself.

423
34:53.536 --> 34:55.296
They're all so pretty. Are you interested?

424
35:01.166 --> 35:02.166
So cute.

425
35:02.616 --> 35:03.516
Pick one.

426
35:03.936 --> 35:05.206
I'll buy it for you

427
35:05.466 --> 35:07.316
as a reward for riding that horse.

428
35:08.726 --> 35:09.906
I won't refuse, then.

429
35:09.926 --> 35:10.926
Mm.

430
35:12.246 --> 35:13.926
They're all pretty.

431
35:16.346 --> 35:17.046
Whoa...

432
35:18.136 --> 35:19.446
I'll have this one.

433
35:20.166 --> 35:20.936
So cute.

434
35:21.536 --> 35:23.126
A bracelet.

435
35:24.726 --> 35:25.606
How much is it?

436
35:25.626 --> 35:26.836
One hundred baht.

437
35:27.476 --> 35:28.236
Thank you.

438
35:31.516 --> 35:32.316
Thank you.

439
35:34.086 --> 35:35.036
Isn't this cute?

440
35:42.236 --> 35:43.416
Open your eyes.

441
35:47.146 --> 35:49.046
I knew it was going to be a bracelet.

442
35:50.446 --> 35:52.236
You're not surprised at all?

443
35:53.436 --> 35:57.026
Well, around seventy percent of the things you've gifted me

444
35:57.536 --> 35:59.336
were bracelets.

445
36:04.406 --> 36:06.386
Well, your wrist is beautiful.

446
36:07.246 --> 36:08.246
Especially...

447
36:10.586 --> 36:11.826
when you do "that."

448
36:14.996 --> 36:15.926
Hey.

449
36:17.236 --> 36:18.186
I'm glad

450
36:18.216 --> 36:19.816
you haven't changed.

451
36:21.126 --> 36:21.626
Here.

452
36:22.626 --> 36:23.526
Let me put it on for you.

453
36:51.146 --> 36:52.206
Sun...

454
36:54.016 --> 36:55.806
You've given me a bracelet before, haven't you?

455
37:07.646 --> 37:08.326
Chris!

456
37:09.646 --> 37:10.726
Chris, what's wrong?

457
37:18.776 --> 37:19.806
Breathe slowly.

458
37:37.386 --> 37:40.956
Didn't you say things would be better if I gave Chris her freedom?

459
37:41.736 --> 37:43.736
So why did she leave me?

460
37:46.336 --> 37:48.706
I'm not happy at all, Jeen.

461
37:50.806 --> 37:52.946
I want her back.

462
38:01.136 --> 38:02.536
Chris called.

463
38:06.376 --> 38:07.436
Jeen,

464
38:08.016 --> 38:10.746
can you convince Chris to come back to me?

465
38:25.076 --> 38:26.116
Hello, Chris.

466
38:26.396 --> 38:27.056
Hello.

467
38:27.516 --> 38:29.336
I want to open the door to my memories.

468
38:30.166 --> 38:31.536
I want to know the truth.

469
38:32.756 --> 38:34.726
I want all of my memories back.

470
38:59.056 --> 39:00.026
Did you finish your call?

471
39:00.546 --> 39:01.546
Shall we go home?

472
39:06.436 --> 39:07.436
Thanks, Sun.

473
39:08.146 --> 39:09.926
I have to apologize

474
39:10.666 --> 39:12.316
for bringing you here

475
39:12.336 --> 39:13.946
and causing you to have a panic attack.

476
39:14.546 --> 39:15.776
Are you even more scared now?

477
39:16.936 --> 39:17.816
I am.

478
39:18.656 --> 39:21.366
But if I don't do anything, nothing will change.

479
39:22.916 --> 39:25.936
Before, just thinking about my parents scared me.

480
39:26.226 --> 39:28.026
But now that I'm here...

481
39:28.416 --> 39:30.366
I want to learn more about them.

482
39:32.636 --> 39:34.596
Even though things ended badly...

483
39:35.046 --> 39:38.206
that doesn't mean we didn't have good memories together.

484
39:42.156 --> 39:43.386
I want to remember everything

485
39:43.936 --> 39:45.816
because of you, Sun.

486
39:47.926 --> 39:48.896
How about

487
39:49.216 --> 39:51.436
visiting your parents' house next trip?

488
39:54.056 --> 39:54.846
Yeah.

489
40:00.846 --> 40:02.116
Thank you so much.

490
40:08.036 --> 40:08.616
Hey.

491
40:09.906 --> 40:10.926
The heart pendant is gone.

492
40:17.846 --> 40:19.946
It might have fallen off when you had a panic attack.

493
40:20.226 --> 40:22.326
It's alright. I'll buy you a new one.

494
40:23.336 --> 40:24.736
It's not the same, Sun.

495
40:30.716 --> 40:31.856
Are you in a rush?

496
40:33.236 --> 40:34.176
Why?

497
40:41.716 --> 40:43.366
[Do not litter on the beach]

498
40:49.906 --> 40:51.226
It has to be around here.

499
40:52.316 --> 40:53.316
Are you serious?

500
40:53.966 --> 40:55.236
It has to be.

501
40:55.446 --> 40:56.506
Where did it go?

502
41:14.726 --> 41:15.726
Your phone!

503
41:20.336 --> 41:22.056
Chris isn't answering my calls.

504
41:22.296 --> 41:24.716
Can you call her for me?

505
41:25.196 --> 41:28.116
Tell her to come get urgent treatment or something.

506
41:29.486 --> 41:30.536
Calm down.

507
41:30.826 --> 41:33.036
Chris already said she wants to remember everything.

508
41:33.416 --> 41:34.926
She'll be back.

509
41:34.946 --> 41:37.336
She'll come back after she's already with someone else?

510
41:42.176 --> 41:43.256
Does she...

511
41:43.516 --> 41:45.036
love you right now, Nadear?

512
41:47.026 --> 41:48.996
If you're not going to help,

513
41:49.026 --> 41:50.366
don't say that to me.

514
41:50.826 --> 41:52.316
I'm saying the truth.

515
41:52.916 --> 41:54.326
Perhaps...

516
41:54.346 --> 41:56.276
it's time for you to admit...

517
41:56.296 --> 41:57.756
Don't stick your nose into this if you're not helping!

518
41:59.146 --> 42:01.836
I'll make her mine again myself.

519
42:03.576 --> 42:04.336
Nadear.

520
42:05.326 --> 42:06.346
Excuse me!

521
42:06.366 --> 42:07.366
Hey!

522
42:08.336 --> 42:09.116
How much per bucket?

523
42:09.136 --> 42:09.976
One hundred each.

524
42:10.406 --> 42:11.626
Two purple buckets, please.

525
42:11.646 --> 42:12.416
Okay.

526
42:14.776 --> 42:16.126
Give me one pink bucket, please.

527
42:16.216 --> 42:17.436
Okay.

528
42:19.196 --> 42:21.226
Why are you doing it alone? Let me join in too.

529
42:26.036 --> 42:27.526
The total is three hundred baht.

530
42:27.546 --> 42:28.916
- I'll scan to pay. - Okay.

531
42:29.636 --> 42:30.396
Done.

532
42:30.416 --> 42:31.246
Thank you.

533
42:36.606 --> 42:38.706
[Third Person Bar - Bistro]

534
42:43.836 --> 42:45.616
Keep your girlfriend in check, why don't you?

535
42:45.846 --> 42:47.366
Don't let her bother me.

536
42:47.876 --> 42:48.976
Or else I'll tell her

537
42:49.416 --> 42:50.926
what you did.

538
42:59.446 --> 43:01.016
Please take this.

539
43:05.516 --> 43:07.416
That bottle is already expired.

540
43:16.006 --> 43:17.626
I can't find it.

541
43:18.546 --> 43:19.486
Sun,

542
43:19.506 --> 43:21.206
how could you lie there? It's dirty.

543
43:21.226 --> 43:22.016
Get up.

544
43:22.046 --> 43:22.636
Come on.

545
43:23.206 --> 43:24.526
Are you WHO or something?

546
43:24.886 --> 43:25.886
- Come here. - Hey.

547
43:28.946 --> 43:31.046
It's okay if you can't find it.

548
43:31.066 --> 43:32.356
You don't have to feel bad about it.

549
43:33.026 --> 43:35.426
You didn't mean to lose it, did you?

550
43:36.426 --> 43:38.896
Well, I've already lost a lot in my life.

551
43:40.046 --> 43:41.736
Whether it's my memories,

552
43:42.416 --> 43:44.316
the people I knew,

553
43:45.936 --> 43:47.036
or even my parents.

554
43:49.316 --> 43:51.926
I don't want to lose anything in my life ever again.

555
43:54.546 --> 43:55.916
If you mean me,

556
43:56.766 --> 43:58.076
I won't go anywhere.

557
44:01.046 --> 44:02.046
Really.

558
44:16.306 --> 44:16.966
Oh!

559
44:20.626 --> 44:21.626
Found it!

560
44:21.846 --> 44:22.846
Whoa!

561
44:23.626 --> 44:24.626
You're good at this.

562
44:24.986 --> 44:26.376
Oh, thank you so much.

563
44:27.426 --> 44:28.256
Are you happy?

564
44:28.276 --> 44:29.186
Mm.

565
44:29.226 --> 44:30.356
It's so hard to find.

566
44:31.066 --> 44:32.116
It's so small.

567
44:32.366 --> 44:33.996
- Thank you. - I have good eyes.

568
44:34.026 --> 44:35.806
Well done.

569
44:36.986 --> 44:41.556
[Third Person]

570
44:42.803 --> 44:46.673
[Third Person]

571
44:59.663 --> 45:00.593
It's a shame, isn't it?

572
45:01.583 --> 45:03.473
We can't see the sunset from this beach.

573
45:05.723 --> 45:09.433
We could have made more beautiful memories together.

574
45:12.173 --> 45:14.273
If we can't watch the sunset together,

575
45:15.793 --> 45:16.953
then...

576
45:22.763 --> 45:24.763
shall we watch the sunrise together?

577
45:35.343 --> 45:38.353
What's that photo? Delete it now.

578
45:39.173 --> 45:40.353
It's cute.

579
45:42.983 --> 45:43.753
Delete it.

580
45:43.773 --> 45:45.753
Hey, don't, Sun.

581
45:45.773 --> 45:48.233
I don't want to lose any photos.

582
45:49.053 --> 45:49.833
Fine.

583
45:50.393 --> 45:52.873
But if you don't have any space, don't come back to erase it.

584
45:53.593 --> 45:54.323
Yes.

585
45:54.703 --> 45:55.403
Give it here.

586
46:00.093 --> 46:01.193
You have a tattoo?

587
46:07.633 --> 46:09.153
Mm. [CN]

588
46:10.573 --> 46:12.013
I can't remember...

589
46:12.463 --> 46:14.153
where I got this from.

590
46:17.243 --> 46:19.793
You probably got it because you loved her a lot.

591
46:30.793 --> 46:32.673
[Nadear]

592
46:43.233 --> 46:45.063
Can you answer my call?

593
46:45.093 --> 46:47.113
I want to talk about our restaurant.

594
46:49.273 --> 46:50.553
You can talk to her.

595
46:50.923 --> 46:51.953
I don't mind.

596
46:54.863 --> 46:55.863
I'll be back.

597
46:56.233 --> 46:57.313
One sec.

598
46:57.813 --> 46:58.393
Mm.

599
46:58.413 --> 46:59.373
I'll be quick.

600
47:03.693 --> 47:04.693
Yes, Nadear?

601
47:05.193 --> 47:06.353
Did something happen at the restaurant?

602
47:07.243 --> 47:08.913
I missed you.

603
47:10.333 --> 47:12.213
It was my fault.

604
47:12.233 --> 47:13.753
I was rushing things.

605
47:14.953 --> 47:16.893
Can you come back to me?

606
47:17.673 --> 47:19.873
Didn't you want to talk about the restaurant?

607
47:20.383 --> 47:22.553
If it's not about our restaurant,

608
47:23.553 --> 47:25.473
would you talk to me?

609
47:27.273 --> 47:28.073
Nadear,

610
47:28.973 --> 47:31.673
whether I talk to you or not, my feelings are the same.

611
47:32.243 --> 47:33.713
Let's not be together.

612
47:34.393 --> 47:36.173
It really isn't going to work out.

613
47:38.283 --> 47:40.593
Why don't we end this on a positive note?

614
47:41.563 --> 47:43.633
If you really want to end it here,

615
47:45.903 --> 47:47.833
I can't stop you.

616
47:50.093 --> 47:51.873
I still want to be your friend, though.

617
47:56.193 --> 47:57.393
I'll hang up now, Nadear.

618
48:07.493 --> 48:09.793
I can't be your friend, Chris.

619
48:29.483 --> 48:30.383
Excuse me,

620
48:30.963 --> 48:32.793
where did the woman at this table go?

621
48:33.053 --> 48:33.653
Oh,

622
48:33.673 --> 48:35.153
she seemed to have left.

623
48:35.463 --> 48:36.463
Huh?

624
48:43.333 --> 48:44.073
Sun!

625
48:45.813 --> 48:46.663
Sun!

626
48:49.673 --> 48:50.673
Sun!

627
48:52.553 --> 48:53.393
Chris!

628
49:02.133 --> 49:03.953
I thought you left me.

629
49:04.223 --> 49:05.853
I just went to get my power bank

630
49:06.493 --> 49:07.493
from the car.

631
49:07.513 --> 49:08.393
I also found...

632
49:08.513 --> 49:10.113
this sugar figurine.

633
49:11.503 --> 49:12.393
Isn't it cute?

634
49:13.663 --> 49:14.843
It's sweet too.

635
49:14.863 --> 49:16.183
Wanna try?

636
49:22.093 --> 49:23.273
You're so much sweeter.

637
49:25.963 --> 49:27.633
Can you not disappear like that again?

638
49:29.803 --> 49:31.313
If you don't want me to disappear,

639
49:31.703 --> 49:33.393
make me yours, then.

640
50:07.913 --> 50:10.433
You know I was just teasing you earlier, right?

641
50:12.083 --> 50:14.033
Even if you're not mine,

642
50:14.983 --> 50:16.353
I won't leave you.

643
50:29.563 --> 50:32.033
I want to make great memories with you here, Sun.

644
50:49.533 --> 50:51.593
A memory I'll never forget.

645
51:05.933 --> 51:07.963
I won't let you forget either.

646
51:26.713 --> 51:29.713
♫Every morning when I see the Sun,♫

647
51:29.733 --> 51:33.263
♫It reminds me of you, hun♫

648
51:33.283 --> 51:37.263
♫Your smile is always so bright♫

649
51:37.283 --> 51:40.993
♫The smile imprinted in my heart♫

650
51:42.253 --> 51:49.263
♫Lost in this hour of romantic reverie♫

651
51:49.283 --> 51:52.673
♫I wish time would stop for me♫

652
51:52.993 --> 51:57.403
♫To cherish this moment♫

653
51:58.723 --> 52:04.253
[CN]

654
52:05.053 --> 52:05.953
Sun.

655
52:06.623 --> 52:10.153
♫Always being near, hugging you tight,♫

656
